eign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act is to be construed, unless the contrary intention appears, as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being. As such, references to ‘Her Majesty’ and ‘the Queen’ have been replaced in the wording of the offences to state ‘His Majesty’ or ‘the King’, although this may not be the strict wording of the legislation.(iv) Childlike sex dolls - whilst there is no specific offence of simply possessing a childlike sex doll there are some potential connected offences. This is one of the possible offences and CPS have provided some useful Legal Guidance which provides the details.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><description>EITHER WAY</description></modeoftrial><timelimitforprosecutions>Complex - see legislation</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>SUMMARY: Six months imprisonment and / or a fine of £20,000 or of three times the value of the goods, whichever is the greater.&lt;br /&gt;INDICTMENT: Seven years imprisonment and / or a fine.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;Complex - see legislation</penalty><geographicregion><code>EW</code><description>England and Wales</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>CE79166</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><pncacpooffencecode>4.10.63.1</pncacpooffencecode><notifiabletoho><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></notifiabletoho><hoclassification>099/23</hoclassification><mopireviewgroup><code>C</code><description>Group 3</description></mopireviewgroup><mopinoteslink>D19586</mopinoteslink><disqualificationclass><code>N</code><description>discretionary disqualifica